-The mod bridges the gap between EMI and the mods from the [Let’s Do] collection, as they only have JEI & REI support natively. It adds in recipes in EMI for all kind of crafting methods provided by mods from the [Let's Do] collection.
+Private NeoForge 1.21.1 compatibility repair, based on MIT-licensed Let's Do EMI Compat 2.0.3, source commit `5c8dad12f3a996b4eab6483e2761e41243368064`. EMI and Architectury are required; the supported content mods remain optional.
 
 
 <details>
@@ -12,18 +12,20 @@
 
 
 
-This mod requires EMI to be installed. It does not require any of the mods from the [Let's Do] collection, so you can opt in or out on any of them.
+## Retained guidance
 
-The mod brings all kinds of recipes into EMI from the following mods:
+- Beachparty mini-fridge and tiki-bar recipes.
+- HerbalBrews cauldron and kettle recipes, including consumed kettle containers in material planning.
+- Bakery cake cutting (install the compatibility jar on both client and server for the custom cake-cut recipe type and data).
+- Meadow 1.4.10 in-world fondue filling and bread dipping. One wheel supplies four portions; a cheese piece supplies one. One bread and one stored portion produce one cheese stick. The pot is reusable, requires heat and active empty-main-hand stirring, and cannot accept another ingredient while melting. A wheel requires an empty pot; pieces fill it one at a time to four portions. Dipping requires no cheese currently melting.
+- Vinery grape-pot guidance: three matching grapes and one empty Vinery Wine Bottle per juice.
 
-- [Let's Do] Bakery
-- [Let's Do] Beachparty
-- [Let's Do] Brewery
-- [Let's Do] Candlelight
-- [Let's Do] Herbal Brews
-- [Let's Do] Meadow
-- [Let's Do] Vinery
-- [Let's Do] Nether Vinery
-- [Let's Do] Farm & Charm & Compat Versions of the mods listed above
-- [Let's Do] Camping
-- [Let's Do] Furniture
+Fondue and grape-pot displays are client-side guidance and add no server recipes. Fondue is deliberately not a recipe-tree source: its stored portions are block-entity state, not obtainable inventory items. No fictitious filled-pot item or bread-only cheese-stick material plan is registered.
+
+Native Bakery, Brewery, Candlelight, Farm & Charm, Meadow cooking/cheese pressing/woodcutting, and Vinery machine recipes are left to their own EMI plugins. Unchanged inactive upstream sources remain in the checkout but are excluded from compilation. Obsolete `fondue_fill`/`fondue_use` serializers and fractional-fill JSON are removed; fondue guidance adds no server recipe data.
+
+## Build and check
+
+Use JDK 21 and the checksum-pinned native dependencies downloaded by `scripts/build-emi-compat.sh` in the pack repository. That builder applies the private source patch, runs `checkRecipeSemantics`, builds the reproducible jar, and prints its SHA-256 for the pack's integrated hash refresh. It never installs jars.
+
+The semantic check constructs a real native kettle recipe, checks its real EMI widget ingredients, and passes it through EMI's material-node consumer to check that consumed containers remain in the plan.
